weak|little-strength|ADJECTIVE|having little strength|Having little physical strength or ability to resist force.|yếu; không chắc|The weak branch bent under the weight of the basket.|Cành cây yếu cong xuống dưới sức nặng của chiếc giỏ.|Used before nouns or after linking verbs; weak can describe a person or material. Weaker and weakest are regular comparative forms.|0
weak|unconvincing|ADJECTIVE|not convincing or effective|Not convincing, effective, or well supported.|yếu; thiếu thuyết phục|His explanation was weak because it ignored the missing receipt.|Lời giải thích của anh thiếu thuyết phục vì bỏ qua tờ biên nhận bị thiếu.|Common with argument, evidence, or explanation; weak on a subject may describe limited knowledge in that area.|1
disgraceful|unacceptably-bad|ADJECTIVE|unacceptably bad or shameful|So bad or unacceptable that it deserves strong disapproval.|đáng xấu hổ; đáng hổ thẹn|The volunteers described the deliberate damage to the memorial as disgraceful.|Các tình nguyện viên cho rằng việc cố ý phá hoại đài tưởng niệm là đáng hổ thẹn.|Used before a noun or after a linking verb; it is disgraceful that introduces a strongly disapproving judgement.|-
heavy|much-weight|ADJECTIVE|having a lot of weight|Having a large weight or being difficult to lift because of its weight.|nặng|The heavy chest needed two people to move it upstairs.|Chiếc rương nặng cần hai người để chuyển lên tầng trên.|Heavier and heaviest change y to i; heavy for someone identifies whose strength or expectations provide the comparison.|0
heavy|large-intensity|ADJECTIVE|large in amount or intensity|Large in amount, force, or intensity.|nhiều; dày đặc; dữ dội|Heavy traffic delayed the bus near the bridge.|Giao thông đông đúc làm xe buýt chậm lại gần cây cầu.|Common with rain, traffic, or workload; heavy rain concerns amount or intensity, not the weight of a single drop.|1
mad|angry|ADJECTIVE|very angry|Very angry or annoyed.|tức giận; bực mình|Tuan was mad at himself for leaving the tickets at home.|Tuấn bực mình với bản thân vì để vé ở nhà.|Informal, especially American; mad at someone or about something. Context distinguishes anger from other uses of mad.|0
mad|foolish-or-unreasonable|ADJECTIVE|foolish or unreasonable|So foolish or unreasonable that it seems to make no sense.|điên rồ; thiếu lý trí|Crossing the flooded path at night would be a mad idea.|Băng qua con đường ngập nước vào ban đêm sẽ là một ý tưởng điên rồ.|Informal evaluation of an idea or action; not a clinical description of a person's mental health.|1
orchestra|instrumental-group|NOUN|large group of instrumental musicians|A large group of musicians who play different instruments together, usually under a conductor.|dàn nhạc|The orchestra tuned its instruments before the audience entered.|Dàn nhạc chỉnh dây và âm thanh của các nhạc cụ trước khi khán giả vào.|Countable collective noun; singular or plural agreement depends on variety and whether the group or its members are emphasized.|0
